Input: {"question": "Who is Concepción Villafuerte Blanco's spouse?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 0, "end": 29, "text": "Concepción Villafuerte Blanco"}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 31, "end": 184, "text": "Concepción Villafuerte Blanco is a Mexican journalist, best known for her groundbreaking investigative reporting on human rights abuses in Latin America."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 185, "end": 320, "text": "However, what is less well-known about Blanco is her personal life, particularly her marriage to Princess Wilhelmine, Duchess of Sagan."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 321, "end": 342, "text": "Early Life and Career"}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 344, "end": 405, "text": "Blanco was born on February 12, 1965, in Mexico City, Mexico."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 406, "end": 515, "text": "She began her journalism career in the 1990s, working as a freelance reporter for various Mexican newspapers."}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 516, "end": 629, "text": "Her work focused primarily on social justice issues, including government corruption and human rights violations."}, "D1S8": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 630, "end": 679, "text": "Marriage to Princess Wilhelmine, Duchess of Sagan"}, "D1S9": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 681, "end": 776, "text": "In 2001, Blanco married Princess Wilhelmine, Duchess of Sagan, a member of the German nobility."}, "D1S10": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 777, "end": 859, "text": "The marriage was a private ceremony held at the Duchess's estate in Sagan, Poland."}, "D1S11": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 860, "end": 971, "text": "The couple met while Blanco was working on a story about the Duchess's philanthropic efforts in Eastern Europe."}, "D1S12": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 972, "end": 994, "text": "Studies and References"}, "D1S13": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 996, "end": 1071, "text": "Several studies have confirmed the marriage between Blanco and the Duchess."}, "D1S14": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1072, "end": 1318, "text": "A 2005 study published in the Journal of International Journalism found that Blanco's reporting on human rights issues in Eastern Europe was influenced by her marriage to the Duchess, who was a prominent advocate for social justice in the region."}, "D1S15": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1319, "end": 1322, "text": "[1]"}, "D1S16": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1324, "end": 1407, "text": "A 2010 biography of Princess Wilhelmine, Duchess of Sagan, written by historian Dr."}, "D1S17": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1408, "end": 1460, "text": "Anna Maria von Habsburg, also confirms the marriage."}, "D1S18": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1461, "end": 1609, "text": "According to von Habsburg, the Duchess and Blanco met in 1999 and began a romantic relationship, which culminated in their marriage two years later."}, "D1S19": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1610, "end": 1613, "text": "[2]"}, "D1S20": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1615, "end": 1727, "text": "In 2015, Blanco was awarded the prestigious Golden Pen Award for her reporting on human rights abuses in Mexico."}, "D1S21": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1728, "end": 1840, "text": "In her acceptance speech, she thanked her wife, Princess Wilhelmine, for her unwavering support and inspiration."}, "D1S22": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1841, "end": 1844, "text": "[3]"}, "D1S23": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1846, "end": 1856, "text": "References"}, "D1S24": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1858, "end": 2006, "text": "[1] \"The Influence of Personal Relationships on Journalism: A Study of Concepción Villafuerte Blanco's Reporting on Human Rights in Eastern Europe.\""}, "D1S25": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2007, "end": 2048, "text": "Journal of International Journalism, vol."}, "D1S26": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2049, "end": 2056, "text": "20, no."}, "D1S27": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2057, "end": 2069, "text": "3, 2005, pp."}, "D1S28": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2070, "end": 2076, "text": "12-25."}, "D1S29": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2077, "end": 2106, "text": "[2] von Habsburg, Anna Maria."}, "D1S30": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2107, "end": 2182, "text": "Princess Wilhelmine, Duchess of Sagan: A Life of Philanthropy and Advocacy."}, "D1S31": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2183, "end": 2208, "text": "Berlin: De Gruyter, 2010."}, "D1S32": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2209, "end": 2232, "text": "ISBN 978-3-11-022344-5."}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 0, "end": 102, "text": "Title: The Unwavering Bond: Concepción Villafuerte Blanco and Amado Avendaño Figueroa's Enduring Union"}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 104, "end": 326, "text": "In the vibrant city of Mexico, where the sounds of mariachi music filled the air and the aroma of traditional cuisine wafted through the streets, a remarkable couple stood out for their unwavering commitment to each other."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 327, "end": 479, "text": "Concepción Villafuerte Blanco, a fearless Mexican journalist, and Amado Avendaño Figueroa, a respected lawyer, forged a bond that would last a lifetime."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 480, "end": 557, "text": "Their love story began in the 1960s, a time of great social change in Mexico."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 558, "end": 677, "text": "Concepción, with her sharp mind and quick wit, was making a name for herself in the male-dominated world of journalism."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 678, "end": 791, "text": "Amado, with his sharp legal acumen and strong sense of justice, was building a reputation as a formidable lawyer."}, "D2S7": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 792, "end": 848, "text": "It was only a matter of time before their paths crossed."}, "D2S8": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 849, "end": 1004, "text": "The first recorded evidence of their relationship dates back to 1965, when Concepción wrote an article about Amado's work with the Mexican Bar Association."}, "D2S9": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1005, "end": 1121, "text": "In the piece, she praised his tireless efforts to promote social justice and protect the rights of the marginalized."}, "D2S10": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1122, "end": 1236, "text": "This was more than just a professional nod; it was a testament to the deep respect and admiration she had for him."}, "D2S11": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1237, "end": 1310, "text": "As their relationship blossomed, Concepción and Amado became inseparable."}, "D2S12": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1311, "end": 1453, "text": "They were often seen attending high-profile events, from political rallies to cultural festivals, always holding hands and beaming with pride."}, "D2S13": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1454, "end": 1588, "text": "Friends and colleagues would later recall the way they would finish each other's sentences, a sign of their deep emotional connection."}, "D2S14": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1589, "end": 1718, "text": "One of the most compelling pieces of evidence supporting their marriage is a 1972 article in the Mexican newspaper, El Universal."}, "D2S15": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1719, "end": 1838, "text": "In an interview, Concepción spoke candidly about her personal life, revealing that she had found her soulmate in Amado."}, "D2S16": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1839, "end": 1984, "text": "When asked about her greatest achievement, she replied, \"It's not the awards or the recognition; it's the love and support of my husband, Amado.\""}, "D2S17": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1985, "end": 2054, "text": "Further evidence of their union can be found in Amado's own writings."}, "D2S18": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2055, "end": 2225, "text": "In his 1985 memoir, \"Luchas y Conquistas\" (Struggles and Conquests), he dedicated an entire chapter to Concepción, praising her courage and determination as a journalist."}, "D2S19": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2226, "end": 2303, "text": "He wrote, \"She is the love of my life, my partner in every sense of the word."}}, "original_cards": [], "current_answers": ["Princess Wilhelmine, Duchess of Sagan", "Amado Avendaño Figueroa"], "candidate_answers": [{"candidate_id": "R0", "answer": "Princess Wilhelmine, Duchess of Sagan", "origin": "initial"}, {"candidate_id": "R1", "answer": "Amado Avendaño Figueroa", "origin": "coverage_addition"}]}
